#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_margin_log.py — fence MARGIN_LOG_20261016
#
# "How much money does each strategy really need?" — record the REAL margin
# of every strategy's open positions while paper (and live) trades run.
#
# BACKEND  backend/app/api/margin_log_routes.py (new)
#   * APScheduler job `margin_log_sampler`, cron */5 Mon–Fri; gated inside to
#     the NFO session (holiday-aware is_market_open) and 09:20–15:25 IST
#     (skips the 09:15 entry/quote burst and the 15:26 exits).
#   * Each pass: for every licensed strategy, its OPEN legs per book (PAPER /
#     LIVE) from fleet_today_routes._legs_for — the dashboard's own reader —
#     → kite.basket_order_margins(consider_positions=False), BUY legs first,
#     NRML. One row per (pass, strategy, book) in app.db `margin_samples`:
#     total, SPAN, exposure, option premium, lots, per lot, every leg.
#     A failed call is stored with its error and the pass continues.
#     Kept 180 days. Places no orders; touches no engine.
#   * Lots = the largest SELL leg (IC 10 shorts + 8 ADJ → 10); buy-only
#     strategies use the largest leg. Per lot = total ÷ lots.
#   * GET  /api/margin-log/summary?days=&book=   per strategy+book median /
#          P90 / peak (+ when, at how many lots) / per-lot, and "fleet at
#          once" per book = Σ over the same pass (what the account must hold)
#     GET  /api/margin-log/samples?days=&strategy_id=&book=   raw rows
#     POST /api/margin-log/sample-now   one manual pass (works off-hours)
# FRONTEND frontend/src/components/MarginLog.jsx (new) on the Paper Trades
#   page, under the trades table: summary table, days / book filters, Sample
#   now, Export CSV. Names via stratName() (non-admin never sees raw ids).
#
#  EDIT  backend/app/api_server.py (import, include_router, scheduler job)
#        frontend/src/pages/PaperTrades.jsx (import, mount)
#  NEW   margin_log_routes.py, test_margin_log.py, MarginLog.jsx
#  Mirrored to desktop/src-tauri/{backend,frontend}/ when those trees exist.
#  Gates: py_compile, esbuild parse, the new suite (35 checks: basket order,
#  lots, per-book rows, failure isolation, 09:20/15:25 gate on the real epoch
#  clock, no-session, summary + fleet-concurrent math, retention, overlap).
#  Any failure → every file restored.
#
# Usage: python3 apply_margin_log.py [--repo PATH] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]
# Run ONLY this script (the new files are carried inside it).

